    "created_at": "2016-07-27T22:15:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-27T22:15:38Z",
    "body": "What should we do on Android, where we can't detect connectability? We could say that the UA MAY treat non-connectable devices as not matching, but we'll definitely have platform divergence and confused developers.\n\nDo we have lots of services that both connectable and non-connectable devices advertise? Or is this just something we're running into because we're trying to write generic applications that target a more varying set of devices than most of our developers will target?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
